results.statement:
\label{prop:model-total-regular}
For every $M\models T$, the functor $G_M$ preserves finite limits,
finite coproducts, and regular images.

\label{lem:ultrapower-regular}
The functor $\mathscr U:\mathbf{Set}\to\mathbf{Set}$ preserves
finite limits, finite coproducts, and regular images.

\label{cor:arithmetic}
\label{thm:arithmetic-comparison-inseparability}
For every consistent c.e.\ extension of PA, its theorem and
refutation sets of sentence codes are recursively inseparable.
Consequently every consistent c.e.\ extension of it is incomplete.

\label{def:sentence-object}
The sentence object $s:S\hookrightarrow\Fm$ is the pullback
\[
\begin{tikzcd}
 S\arrow[r,hook,"s"]\arrow[d] & \Fm\arrow[d,"\FV_{\Fm}"]\\
 1\arrow[r,"\nil"'] & W.
\end{tikzcd}
\]
